    /// <summary>
    /// A vertex moved of a closed multiline MLEDIT has cut (<c>DxfMlineBuilder.MoveVertexAt</c>, which a grip and STRETCH use)
    /// against the records AutoCAD 2021 left, as <see cref="MlineMoveVertexOnClosedCutTests"/> does it: the rows are the
    /// triangle 0,0 100,0 50,80 cut across its last vertex, the six-sided staircase 0,0 100,0 100,50 50,50 50,100 0,100 cut
    /// across its last vertex and across vertex 3, and MLEDIT's cuts of the staircase that end exactly at the end of an
    /// element. AutoCAD puts a nought in front of the list that goes on from the segment before (the cut across a vertex)
    /// when a move makes that segment whole only for the vertices between the first and the one before the last, not for the
    /// first or the last, which join the end of the points to their start: the triangle cut across vertex 2 and moved at
    /// vertex 1 or 2 keeps (50,80){47.1699} where the square, cut across vertex 1 or 2 of four, writes {0,...}. A cut that
    /// runs to the end of an element is written without the stretch that would start there: a cut from 35 of an element 50
    /// long is <c>{0,35}</c> and not <c>{0,35,50}</c>.
    /// </summary>
    public class MlineMoveVertexClosedEndsTests
